## What Problem This Solves

Plugin authors and channel extensions currently duplicate reply-session initialization conflict classification using ad hoc regex and manual error.message checks. Without a shared, stable classifier, any change to the error message breaks hard-to-find classification logic across Discord, Signal, Slack, Telegram, and WhatsApp. The Plugin SDK should expose a single predicate that extensions import and trust.

## Summary

- expose `isReplySessionInitConflictError(error: unknown)` through
  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/error-runtime`;
- move the conflict error identity into a lightweight shared module;
- replace duplicated classification logic in Discord, Signal, Slack,
  Telegram, and WhatsApp;
- update the Plugin SDK API baseline, surface budget, and subpath docs.

## Behavior

The shared predicate recognizes:

- `ReplySessionInitConflictError` instances;
- strictly matched legacy conflict messages;
- raw legacy message strings;
- wrapped conflicts in `cause` and `error` chains;
- compatible error-like objects with an exact message.

It intentionally does not classify name-only or partial-message matches.

This normalizes wrapped-error handling and strict message matching across
channels. Retry counts, backoff, terminal behavior, and user-facing messages
are unchanged (Discord retry was already removed upstream; wrapping now
correctly routes to terminal notice).

## Evidence

### Unit tests

- classifier tests: 25/25 (typed error, legacy message, raw string,
  cause-chain wrapping, error-like objects, no-throw contract, Proxy traps);
- Plugin SDK export-contract tests: 6/6;
- Discord: 138/138 (includes new wrapped-conflict test);
- Signal: 7/7;
- Slack: 13/13;
- WhatsApp: 54/54;
- Telegram: 115/118 (3 pre-existing Windows path-separator failures).

### Static checks

- `pnpm tsgo:core` — ✅;
- `pnpm check:test-types` — ✅;
- `pnpm build:plugin-sdk:strict-smoke` — ✅ (4/4 exports);
- `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` — ✅;
- `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check` — ✅ (8150 public / 4534 callable);
- `pnpm deadcode:knip` — ✅;
- `pnpm deadcode:exports` — ✅;
- `pnpm check:import-cycles` — 0 cycles;
- `pnpm check:madge-import-cycles` — 0 cycles;
- `npx oxfmt --check` — 15 files correct;
- `git diff --check` — clean.

Four unrelated Windows-only failures were reproduced unchanged on the
upstream/main baseline: one SQLite EBUSY cleanup failure and three Telegram
path-separator assertions.

## Scope

- no retry or backoff changes;
- no terminal-notice changes;
- no new error code;
- no changes to PR #108899;
- QQBot migration is deferred until #108899 is merged.
